      continue to pay your Medicare Part B premium.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <h4>No securities or investment advice</h4>
      <p class="mb0">Roosevelt Brown Jr. is a licensed Life &amp; Health insurance agent in the State of
      Georgia (License {{LIC}}). He is not currently a registered investment adviser, an investment adviser
      representative, or a registered representative of a broker&#8209;dealer, and does not offer securities,
      investment advisory services, tax advice or legal advice. Nothing on this site should be construed as
      such advice. Consult a qualified professional for those matters.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt3">Non-discrimination and accessibility of services</h2>
    <p>We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, disability, sex, religion or
    any other protected class in the provision of services. If you need assistance in another language, or need
    materials in an alternate format such as large print, please contact us at {{PHONE}} and we will
    accommodate your request.</p>

    <h2 class="mt3">How we handle marketing compliance</h2>
    <p>Medicare marketing is governed by the CMS Medicare Communications and Marketing Guidelines, which
    change annually, as well as by individual carrier and FMO requirements and Georgia insurance regulations.
    Our internal process:</p>
    <ol class="steps mt2">
      <li><h4>Classify the material</h4><p>Every public-facing item is first classified as either
      "communication" or "marketing" under current CMS definitions. Material that mentions plan benefits,
      costs, star ratings, or specific carriers is treated as marketing.</p></li>
      <li><h4>Carrier and FMO review</h4><p>Marketing material is submitted to the applicable carrier or FMO for
      review and, where required, for CMS submission through HPMS, before publication.</p></li>
      <li><h4>Required disclaimers applied</h4><p>The multi-plan disclaimer, the government non-affiliation
      statement, and any carrier-specific language are applied before anything goes live.</p></li>
      <li><h4>Retention</h4><p>Approved copies, approval correspondence, approval identifiers and publication
      dates are retained per carrier and CMS retention requirements.</p></li>
      <li><h4>Annual re-review</h4><p>The entire site is re-reviewed each year before the Annual Enrollment
      Period against the current plan-year guidelines, and dated disclosures are updated.</p></li>
      <li><h4>Prompt correction</h4><p>Any item identified as non-compliant is taken down or corrected
      immediately, and the correction is documented.</p></li>
    </ol>

    <div class="panel panel--green">
      <h4>Scope of contact</h4>
      <p class="mb0">When you contact us about Medicare, we will discuss only the plan types and products you
      ask about. We do not make unsolicited contact in violation of CMS rules, and we obtain the required
      permission to contact and scope of appointment documentation before any Medicare sales appointment.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt3">Report a concern</h2>
    <p>If you believe any material on this site is inaccurate, misleading, or non-compliant, please tell us at
    {{EMAIL}} or {{PHONE}}. You may also contact Medicare directly at 1&#8209;800&#8209;MEDICARE, or the
    Georgia Office of Commissioner of Insurance and Safety Fire.</p>

    <p class="small muted">Page last reviewed: <span class="ph">[DATE]</span> &middot; Applicable plan year:
    <span class="ph">[YEAR]</span></p>
  </div>
</section>
""")

