    <h2>Health information</h2>
    <p>Health-related information you provide is treated as confidential and used only to determine suitable
    coverage and submit applications you have authorized. <span class="ph">[Confirm with counsel whether and
    how HIPAA applies to your specific activities, and align this section with your carrier agreements.]</span></p>

    <h2>Text messages and calls</h2>
    <p>If you provide a phone number and consent to contact, we may call or text you about your request.
    Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out of texts. Consent to receive calls or texts is not
    a condition of purchasing anything. We honor the National Do Not Call Registry and applicable TCPA
    requirements. <span class="ph">[Confirm your actual calling, texting and consent-capture practices with
    counsel.]</span></p>

    <h2>Data security and retention</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical and physical safeguards to protect your information. No
    method of transmission or storage is completely secure. We retain records for as long as needed to service
    you and to satisfy carrier, CMS and state retention requirements &mdash; typically
    <span class="ph">[RETENTION PERIOD, commonly 10 years for Medicare records]</span>.</p>

    <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to, correction of, or deletion of the personal information we hold, subject to our
      legal and regulatory retention obligations</li>
      <li>Unsubscribe from marketing emails using the link in any message</li>
      <li>Opt out of text messages by replying STOP</li>
      <li>Ask us not to call you</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these, contact {{EMAIL}} or {{PHONE}}. <span class="ph">[If you serve residents of
    states with comprehensive privacy laws, add the required state-specific rights sections.]</span></p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This website is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal
    information.</p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>We link to sites such as Medicare.gov and HealthCare.gov for your convenience. We are not responsible
    for their content or privacy practices.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be posted here with a revised effective date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: {{EMAIL}} &middot; {{PHONE}} &middot; {{ADDR}}</p>
  </div>
</section>
""")

page("privacy.html", "Privacy Policy",
     "How Southern Comprehensive Insurance, LLC collects, uses, shares and protects your personal information.",
     privacy)


# =====================================================================
# 13. TERMS
# =====================================================================
terms = T(pagehead("Terms of Use", "The rules for using this website.",
  "Plain-language terms covering what this site is, what it isn't, and the limits of what we promise here.") + """
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
""" + LEGAL_NOTE + """
    <p class="small muted">Effective date: <span class="ph">[DATE]</span></p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
    <p>By accessing or using this website you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please do not
    use the site.</p>

    <h2>2. What this site is</h2>
    <p>This website provides general educational information about insurance products and is operated by
    Southern Comprehensive Insurance, LLC, a licensed independent insurance agency in Georgia.</p>

    <h2>3. Not advice, not an offer, not coverage</h2>
    <p>Nothing on this site is insurance, legal, tax, medical or investment advice, nor an offer to sell or a
    solicitation to buy any product in any jurisdiction where we are not licensed. No coverage is bound,
    applied for, or in force through this website. Coverage exists only when an application is approved by a
    carrier and a policy is issued. Content is not a complete description of benefits; policy documents
    control in all cases.</p>

    <h2>4. Calculators and estimates</h2>
    <p>The coverage calculator, cost estimator and any similar tools produce educational estimates using
    generalized assumptions. They are not quotes, offers, recommendations or guarantees. Actual premiums and
    coverage depend on underwriting, carrier filings, your health, your location and other factors. Do not
    make a financial decision on the basis of these tools alone.</p>

    <h2>5. Licensing</h2>
    <p>Roosevelt Brown Jr. is licensed as a Life &amp; Health insurance producer in the State of Georgia
    (License {{LIC}}) <span class="ph">[AND ANY ADDITIONAL STATES]</span>. Products and services are offered
    only where properly licensed and appointed.</p>

    <h2>6. Accuracy and changes</h2>
    <p>We work to keep this site accurate, but insurance rules, plan benefits and premiums change frequently
    and content may become outdated. We may modify or remove content at any time without notice. Verify
    current Medicare information at <a href="https://www.medicare.gov">Medicare.gov</a> or by calling
    1&#8209;800&#8209;MEDICARE, and current Marketplace information at
    <a href="https://www.healthcare.gov">HealthCare.gov</a>.</p>

    <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>The content, design, logo and marks on this site are owned by Southern Comprehensive Insurance, LLC or
    its licensors and may not be copied or reused without written permission. Carrier names and logos are the
    property of their respective owners.</p>

    <h2>8. Third-party links</h2>
    <p>Links to other sites are provided for convenience. We do not control and are not responsible for their
    content, accuracy or practices.</p>

    <h2>9. Your conduct</h2>
    <p>You agree not to use this site unlawfully, to submit false information, to attempt to gain unauthorized
    access to any part of it, or to interfere with its operation or security.</p>

    <h2>10. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>This site is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
    including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement, to the fullest extent
