# =====================================================================
# 14. ACCESSIBILITY
# =====================================================================
access = T(pagehead("Accessibility Statement", "This site should work for everyone.",
  "A large share of the people we serve are seniors, and many use assistive technology. Accessibility "
  "is not an afterthought here.") + """
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <p class="small muted">Last reviewed: <span class="ph">[DATE]</span></p>

    <h2>Our commitment</h2>
    <p>Southern Comprehensive Insurance, LLC is committed to making this website usable by the widest possible
    audience, including people with visual, hearing, cognitive and motor disabilities. We aim to conform to
    the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA.</p>

    <h2>What we've built in</h2>
    <ul class="check">
      <li>Semantic HTML structure with landmarks, correct heading order and descriptive page titles</li>
      <li>A "skip to main content" link for keyboard and screen reader users</li>
      <li>Full keyboard navigation with a clearly visible focus indicator on every interactive element</li>
      <li>Text and interface colors tested to meet WCAG AA contrast ratios</li>
      <li>Body text at 17px with generous line spacing, and layouts that reflow when text is enlarged to 200%</li>
      <li>Every form field paired with a visible, programmatically associated label</li>
      <li>Meaningful alternative text on images, and decorative elements hidden from assistive technology</li>
      <li>Touch targets sized for comfortable use on phones and tablets</li>
      <li>Reduced-motion support that respects your operating system preference</li>
      <li>Content written in plain language, tested to avoid unnecessary jargon</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>Some third-party content we embed &mdash; such as maps, scheduling tools, review widgets and video
    players &mdash; is outside our direct control and may not fully meet WCAG 2.1 AA. Where that happens, we
    provide an alternative way to get the same information or complete the same task. If you hit a barrier,
    call us and a person will help you directly.</p>
    <p class="small muted"><span class="ph">[Update this section after a full audit. Document any known
    issues and the target date for fixing them.]</span></p>

    <h2>Getting help another way</h2>
    <p>If any part of this site is difficult for you to use, you never have to use it. Call {{PHONE}} and we
    will walk you through anything on this website by phone, in person, or in an alternate format including
    large print. There is no charge and no difference in the service you receive.</p>

    <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
    <p>We want to know. Please contact us with the page address, what you were trying to do, and the assistive
    technology or browser you were using:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email: {{EMAIL}}</li>
      <li>Phone: {{PHONE}}</li>
      <li>Mail: {{ADDR}}</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to respond within <span class="ph">[NUMBER]</span> business days and to fix confirmed barriers
    promptly.</p>

    <h2>Ongoing work</h2>
    <p>We review accessibility whenever we make substantial changes, and at minimum annually alongside our
    compliance review. Accessibility is treated as part of the build, not a patch applied afterward.</p>
  </div>
</section>
""")

page("accessibility.html", "Accessibility Statement",
     "Southern Comprehensive Insurance, LLC's commitment to WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility, what we've built in, "
     "known limitations, and how to get help another way.",
     access)

print("\nAll pages generated.")
